        'Along the coasts of eastern India, where rivers meet the sea, grow forests unlike any others. Mangrove trees stand on stilt-like roots in salty mud that is covered by the tide twice a day. Most plants would die in such water, but mangroves have learnt to push out extra salt through their leaves and to breathe through roots that poke up out of the mud.',
